an explicit check might give clearer messaging -- but since the test only verifies that an error occurs rather than its exact text, I can proceed.\n\nSince Go maps gracefully handle missing keys on append, a missing dependency just never gets processed, leaving its in-degree non-zero and naturally surfacing as a cycle—though I'd rather detect missing deps explicitly for clearer errors. Duplicate deps in a node's list aren't worth special-casing here.\n\nWriting the graph package...\n\nProcessing the queue with sorted order, repeatedly popping the alphabetically first ready node, decrementing dependents' in-degree, and merging newly ready nodes back into the sorted queue until empty.\n\nNow I need to check for cycles by comparing result length against the graph size, then move to building the parse.go file that loads JSON node data into a graph structure, validating each node has a name.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":14466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1292},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c705c6f-3d60-45bb-91c8-e7bd805c7381","uuid":"011bceca-452b-4649-8328-78c3207d7a7b"}
